2. Photos and videos
With your permission, SecLery accesses photos, videos and related information, such as capture dates shown in the gallery and used to filter by year. Access is limited to what you permit in your device settings. You can change or revoke access there. SecLery does not upload your media to the provider's servers. If iCloud Photos is enabled, Apple's photo library may download media from iCloud to your device. This is part of Apple's photo library service, not cloud storage operated by SecLery.

3. Authentication and previews
Features such as revealing previews, leaving protected viewing or sharing media may require confirmation through your device's security features. Depending on your device and settings, this can use a fingerprint, facial recognition or a device passcode. The operating system verifies your identity. SecLery receives the result, not your biometric templates or passcode. Unlocked previews stay unlocked only for the current app session unless you lock them again.

4. Sharing and local files
When you share files, SecLery hands them to the system share menu. You choose the destination app, service or recipient. Its privacy information then applies to its handling of the files. Viewing or sharing may create local cache files or temporary copies. SecLery does not transfer these files to the provider's servers. You can remove local app data through device settings where supported or by fully uninstalling the app. This does not delete items in your photo library or copies that you have already shared.

5. Advertising, tracking and external links
This version contains no ads and uses no advertising ID, app tracking or in-app usage analytics. No account is required. Opening a legal link takes you to an external webpage in your browser. GitHub may process information such as your IP address and technical access data. SecLery does not pass photos or videos when opening these links.
GitHub Privacy Statement: https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement

6. Email enquiries
If you contact the provider, they process your email address, message and any attachments you choose to send in order to handle the enquiry. Please do not send private media or other sensitive information unless it is needed for your request. Article 6(1)(b) GDPR applies to enquiries about entering into or performing a contract. Article 6(1)(f) GDPR applies to general enquiries. The legitimate interest is responding to and documenting your enquiry. Enquiries are deleted once no longer needed for that purpose unless statutory retention requirements or the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims require further retention.

7. Your rights
Subject to the applicable legal conditions, you have rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing and data portability. Where processing is based on legitimate interests, you may object on grounds relating to your particular situation. You may withdraw any consent you gave with effect for the future. Use the email address above to exercise your rights. You may also lodge a complaint with a data protection authority, such as the State Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of Information for North Rhine-Westphalia: https://www.ldi.nrw.de/kontakt/ihre-beschwerde

